<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.aditya.dotfiles.qt-scale-factor</string>

  <!-- One job: make Qt apps honour a UI scale, because Anki 26.9.3 will not.
       Its Tools > Preferences > "User interface size" box saves the value
       correctly (uiScale lands in prefs21.db) and then does nothing with it:
       the version sets QT_SCALE_FACTOR *after* constructing the Qt app, so Qt
       has already sized every widget by the time the number arrives. Upstream
       bug, not a local misconfiguration:

         https://github.com/ankitects/anki/issues/5676

       Setting the variable here means it is already in the environment when
       Anki starts, which is the one thing the bug prevents Anki from doing for
       itself. Anki's own late assignment then writes the same value and is
       harmless.

       No shell wrapper: launchctl takes the value directly, there is no logic
       to host, and $HOME is not needed.

       1.3 to match what the preference pane was set to. Change the number here
       and re-run install.d/84-qt-scale-factor.sh; the preference pane itself is
       inert in this version, so this file is the only knob that does anything.
       Higher is bigger -- 1.6 is about right if a 32-inch panel still reads
       small at 1.3. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/launchctl</string>
    <string>setenv</string>
    <string>QT_SCALE_FACTOR</string>
    <string>1.3</string>
  </array>

  <!-- The whole point: set it at login, before anything is launched by hand.
       Nothing here races Anki, because Anki is not a login item -- see
       install.d/85-login-items.sh, which starts other things and not this one.
       An app already running when this fires keeps its old scale until it is
       restarted; at login there is nothing running yet. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- No KeepAlive. launchctl setenv returns immediately, and a KeepAlive on a
       job that exits cleanly is a restart loop. No WatchPaths either: the
       variable is wanted for the whole session, not in response to a file. -->

  <!-- Not scoped to Anki. QT_SCALE_FACTOR is read by every Qt application, so
       any other Qt app launched after login is scaled too. Anki is the only one
       installed here (Brewfile has no other Qt cask), and scoping to one app
       would mean a wrapper bundle for something the Dock launches directly --
       more machinery than the problem is worth.

       Retire this once Anki 26.11 ships, which carries the upstream fix (PR
       #5686, "apply the UI scale before creating the Qt app"). Retiring means
       naming the label in install.d/90-retired-agents.sh, not just deleting
       this file: a copy already in ~/Library/LaunchAgents stays loaded. -->

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
